# LF everywhere, and this is a gate rather than a preference.
#
# src/testing/channel-vectors.json and src/channels/grammar.ts are the client half of a
# contract whose other half is Go, in the private repository revenexx/talkback. The
# intent is for a CI job there to check this repository out, compare
# channel-vectors.json BYTE FOR BYTE against what the Go generator produces, and read
# grammar.ts line by line. That job is not wired up yet, and this rule still has to hold
# before it is: under core.autocrlf=true a checkout would rewrite both files, and the
# comparison would fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the grammar it guards.
# Do not drop this rule.
* text=auto eol=lf
